<title>UK: Claremont gains on soccer clothing deal.</title>
<headline>Claremont gains on soccer clothing deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Claremont Garments Plc rose on Monday after a report in Saturday's Financial Times that the company is to supply Marks &amp; Spencer Plc with soccer clothing under a licensing deal with the Premier League.</p>
<p>The stock was up 9p at 212-1/2 by 0850 GMT in thin trading of 72,300 shares. It fell to a 4-1/2 year low of 202-1/2p on September 27.  </p>
<p>The FT report said the clothing was expected to generate first-year sales of at least 5.0 million stg, after sales of 500,000 stg in the four weeks since its launch without publicity in 50 M&amp;S stores.</p>
<p>No one from the company was immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
